WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.266 --> 00:00:02.702
-You were kind enough to send me
a cut of this last month.

00:00:02.702 --> 00:00:04.004 align:start size:94% position:6%
This is such
a wonderful special.

00:00:04.004 --> 00:00:05.238 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Oh, thank you.
I'm glad you liked that.

00:00:05.238 --> 00:00:07.307
-It is you. It is some other
adult guest stars, like --

00:00:07.307 --> 00:00:10.844 align:start size:94% position:6%
people like Richard Kind,
Natasha, and Jake Gyllenhaal

00:00:10.844 --> 00:00:12.445 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Yeah.
-But mostly it's kids.

00:00:12.445 --> 00:00:16.116 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Oh, yeah, it's me and 15 kids
ages 8 to 13.

00:00:16.116 --> 00:00:19.452 align:start size:94% position:6%
-And why did you have this ide
to work with children?

00:00:19.452 --> 00:00:22.489 align:start size:94% position:6%
-I thought it would be funny
and I had --

00:00:22.489 --> 00:00:24.190 line:92%
I needed something to do.

00:00:24.190 --> 00:00:25.091 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
[ Laughter ]

00:00:25.091 --> 00:00:26.960 align:start size:94% position:6%
And Marika Sawyer,
who you know very well.

00:00:26.960 --> 00:00:29.029
-Yes, a fantastic writer.
-Amazing comedy writer

00:00:29.029 --> 00:00:31.464 align:start size:94% position:6%
who I worked with at
"Saturday Night Live" a lot.

00:00:31.464 --> 00:00:34.334 align:start size:94% position:6%
We always wanted
to write for kids.

00:00:34.334 --> 00:00:38.905
We wanted them to add kids t
the cast of "SNL" at one point

00:00:38.905 --> 00:00:41.141 align:start size:94% position:6%
and have, like, a little updat
that they would cut to.

00:00:41.141 --> 00:00:43.410 align:start size:94% position:6%
So they'd go from Seth and Amy
to two kids, remember?

00:00:43.410 --> 00:00:45.845 align:start size:94% position:6%
And Lorne was like,
"We're not doing that."

00:00:45.845 --> 00:00:46.379 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
[ Laughter ]

00:00:46.379 --> 00:00:52.385
So we had this idea, and then
just started thinking abou

00:00:52.385 --> 00:00:55.321 line:92%
writing kids talking like me

00:00:55.321 --> 00:00:57.424 line:92%
And I thought that's great

00:00:57.424 --> 00:00:58.858 size:88% position:44% line:92%
So there's some of that.

00:00:58.858 --> 00:01:00.627 align:start size:94% position:6%
And then there's
big musical numbers.

00:01:00.627 --> 00:01:01.928 align:start size:94% position:6%
You know,
keep people entertained.

00:01:01.928 --> 00:01:02.695 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Yeah.
[ Laughter ]

00:01:02.695 --> 00:01:07.000 align:start size:94% position:6%
-And then we also interviewe
them a lot on camera.

00:01:07.000 --> 00:01:08.735
-That is --
I mean, the songs are fantastic.

00:01:08.735 --> 00:01:10.303
And I'm not
the least bit surprised by that.

00:01:10.303 --> 00:01:12.505
But one of the parts that really
resonates is the kids

00:01:12.505 --> 00:01:14.174 align:start size:94% position:6%
talk directly to camera,
you hear your voice,

00:01:14.174 --> 00:01:16.009 size:84% position:42%
you hear Rhys Thomas,
the wonderful director.

00:01:16.009 --> 00:01:18.144 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Yeah, Rhys Thomas,
our director, yeah.

00:01:18.144 --> 00:01:18.711 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
-America's voice.

00:01:18.711 --> 00:01:19.746 align:start size:94% position:6%
And a lot of
what they talk about

00:01:19.746 --> 00:01:20.547 line:92%
is the things they're afraid of.

00:01:20.547 --> 00:01:23.817
-Yes, we asked them what their
biggest fears were and then --

00:01:23.817 --> 00:01:26.252 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Were you surprised by
their answers?

00:01:26.252 --> 00:01:28.721 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Yeah, because --
[ Laughter ]

00:01:28.721 --> 00:01:32.158 align:start size:94% position:6%
Do you know, like --
I thought like -- It's 2019.

00:01:32.158 --> 00:01:34.294 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
I was born in 1982.

00:01:34.294 --> 00:01:37.030 line:92%
So, you know, like when I was 7,

00:01:37.030 --> 00:01:39.232 align:start size:94% position:6%
everyone was afraid of,
like, tarantulas, you know

00:01:39.232 --> 00:01:39.666 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
-Yeah.

00:01:39.666 --> 00:01:43.236 align:start size:94% position:6%
-And I wonder what kids in 201
are afraid of.

00:01:43.236 --> 00:01:45.638
And, like, you can speculate
from the news and everything

00:01:45.638 --> 00:01:48.575 align:start size:94% position:6%
And a lot of kids are stil
afraid of tarantulas.

00:01:48.575 --> 00:01:49.809 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Yeah.
-And I don't know why.

00:01:49.809 --> 00:01:53.246
Like, they're really not a thing
you come into contact with

00:01:53.246 --> 00:01:54.280 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Yeah.
[ Laughter ]

00:01:54.280 --> 00:01:55.215 line:92%
Certainly not in New York City

00:01:55.215 --> 00:01:58.284
I want to point out, this is
everybody at the premiere.

00:01:58.284 --> 00:01:59.486 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Oh, yes.
-Which is fantastic.

00:01:59.486 --> 00:02:01.855
They all dressed up.
And when I first met you, you --

00:02:01.855 --> 00:02:04.390 size:78% position:39%
-Sorry, they demanded
that it be black tie.

00:02:04.390 --> 00:02:04.924 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
[ Laughter ]

00:02:04.924 --> 00:02:06.426 align:start size:94% position:6%
We were on set one day in July
and they went,

00:02:06.426 --> 00:02:08.261 align:start size:94% position:6%
"Is there going to
be a premiere?"

00:02:08.261 --> 00:02:08.995 size:84% position:42% line:92%
And I was like, "Yeah."

00:02:08.995 --> 00:02:10.964 align:start size:94% position:6%
And they're like,
"With a red carpet?"

00:02:10.964 --> 00:02:11.698 size:84% position:42% line:92%
And I was like, "Yeah."

00:02:11.698 --> 00:02:13.766 align:start size:94% position:6%
And they're like,
"And everyone dresses fancy?

00:02:13.766 --> 00:02:15.635 align:start size:94% position:6%
And I was like,
"Alright, yeah."

00:02:15.635 --> 00:02:16.202 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
[ Laughter ]

00:02:16.202 --> 00:02:18.438
-I like this because I feel like
when I first met you,

00:02:18.438 --> 00:02:19.839 line:92%
you sometimes looked like a ki

00:02:19.839 --> 00:02:22.142 align:start size:94% position:6%
who was dressed up
like an adult.

00:02:22.142 --> 00:02:22.609 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
-Yes. Yes.

00:02:22.609 --> 00:02:24.544 align:start size:94% position:6%
-And it's fun to see
what that actually looks like.

00:02:24.544 --> 00:02:27.680 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Yes, this was me on an averag
show night, yeah.

00:02:27.680 --> 00:02:29.516 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
[ Laughter ]

00:02:29.516 --> 00:02:32.685 align:start size:94% position:6%
-What was it like
auditioning them?

00:02:32.685 --> 00:02:35.221 line:92%
-Oh, well -- it was -- it was --

00:02:35.221 --> 00:02:38.024 align:start size:94% position:6%
You know, it started off
like 50 or 60 kids.

00:02:38.024 --> 00:02:41.161 align:start size:94% position:6%
And we would have --
They'd come in and do a song

00:02:41.161 --> 00:02:44.164 align:start size:94% position:6%
And sometimes a kid would --
you could tell like,

00:02:44.164 --> 00:02:47.300 align:start size:94% position:6%
"Oh, she might be good at this
type of energy.

00:02:47.300 --> 00:02:48.434 align:start size:94% position:6%
So sometimes we'd
assign them a song.

00:02:48.434 --> 00:02:52.071 align:start size:94% position:6%
So this very talented youn
girl, Lexie, we told her to do

00:02:52.071 --> 00:02:54.440 align:start size:94% position:6%
"You Oughta Know"
by Alanis Morisette.

00:02:54.440 --> 00:02:55.909 size:88% position:44% line:92%
And we told her parents,

00:02:55.909 --> 00:02:58.311 align:start size:94% position:6%
"Could you have her prepar
'You Oughta Know'?"

00:02:58.311 --> 00:02:59.879 line:92%
And she came in and she said

00:02:59.879 --> 00:03:01.981 align:start size:94% position:6%
"I have 'You Oughta Know'
to sing by Alanis Morisette.

00:03:01.981 --> 00:03:03.449 align:start size:94% position:6%
And we were like, "Great,"
and she's like,

00:03:03.449 --> 00:03:05.251 align:start size:94% position:6%
"But just the appropriate
parts," and I was --

00:03:05.251 --> 00:03:06.553 align:start size:94% position:6%
[ Laughter ]
I was like, "What?"

00:03:06.553 --> 00:03:08.621 align:start size:94% position:6%
And she's like,
"Just the appropriate parts.

00:03:08.621 --> 00:03:12.325 align:start size:94% position:6%
And I was like, "Oh!
Yeah, yeah, don't, yeah."

00:03:12.325 --> 00:03:14.294 align:start size:94% position:6%
[ Laughter ]
-You forgot.

00:03:14.294 --> 00:03:17.697 align:start size:94% position:6%
-I forgot the whole point
of the song.

00:03:17.697 --> 00:03:18.464 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
[ Laughter ]

00:03:18.464 --> 00:03:20.667 line:92%
Then we talked to them, like

00:03:20.667 --> 00:03:22.969 align:start size:94% position:6%
just kind of loosely
interview style.

00:03:22.969 --> 00:03:26.039 align:start size:94% position:6%
I gave them --
I had a couple of questions.

00:03:26.039 --> 00:03:29.242 align:start size:94% position:6%
And then there was one round
of kids where I'd say,

00:03:29.242 --> 00:03:32.845 align:start size:94% position:6%
"Fill in the blank --
America has a lot of blank."

00:03:32.845 --> 00:03:34.981 align:start size:94% position:6%
And so I'd say,
"America has a lot of...",

00:03:34.981 --> 00:03:36.816 align:start size:94% position:6%
And some kids said, like,
"hamburgers."

00:03:36.816 --> 00:03:39.285 align:start size:94% position:6%
And some kids would choke
and be like, "Uh..."

00:03:39.285 --> 00:03:40.753 align:start size:94% position:6%
And some kids would say,
"people."

00:03:40.753 --> 00:03:42.755 align:start size:94% position:6%
And this kid, Alex Bello,
who's very talented,

00:03:42.755 --> 00:03:45.992 align:start size:94% position:6%
who's in the special -- I said
"America has a lot of..."

00:03:45.992 --> 00:03:47.293 line:92%
And he said, "Work to do."

00:03:47.293 --> 00:03:51.431 line:92%
[ Laughter and applause ]

00:03:51.431 --> 00:03:54.434 align:start size:94% position:6%
-You talked -- I think it wa
your last special about

00:03:54.434 --> 00:03:57.971
how you were not going to --
you don't want to have kids.

00:03:57.971 --> 00:03:58.938 size:84% position:42% line:92%
-Yeah. Do you have any?

00:03:58.938 --> 00:04:00.807 align:start size:94% position:6%
-I have a couple, yeah.
-Yeah.

00:04:00.807 --> 00:04:02.275 align:start size:94% position:6%
[ Laughter ]
-Sometimes I do.

00:04:02.275 --> 00:04:03.243 line:92%
Most of the time I'm happy

00:04:03.243 --> 00:04:04.877 align:start size:94% position:6%
Sometimes I wished
I'd talk to you.

00:04:04.877 --> 00:04:06.045 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Yeah, yeah.
[ Laughter ]

00:04:06.045 --> 00:04:07.480 line:92%
You wish you had more free time.

00:04:07.480 --> 00:04:09.549
-You've talked to them about it,
though.

00:04:09.549 --> 00:04:11.251 align:start size:94% position:6%
I mean, they must
have been curious.

00:04:11.251 --> 00:04:15.421 align:start size:94% position:6%
-One time on set,
we were holding for a while.

00:04:15.421 --> 00:04:19.025 align:start size:94% position:6%
And they said to me,
"So you don't want kids?"

00:04:19.025 --> 00:04:20.460 line:92%
And I said, "No, no, I don't."

00:04:20.460 --> 00:04:23.329 align:start size:94% position:6%
And then we had
a conversation about it

00:04:23.329 --> 00:04:25.064 size:88% position:44% line:92%
as if they weren't kids.

00:04:25.064 --> 00:04:25.598 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
[ Laughter ]

00:04:25.598 --> 00:04:26.399 line:92%
They were like, "Why not?"

00:04:26.399 --> 00:04:28.334 align:start size:94% position:6%
And I was like,
"Well, my wife and I

00:04:28.334 --> 00:04:29.435 line:92%
really enjoy our time together

00:04:29.435 --> 00:04:31.504 align:start size:94% position:6%
And I like having my free time
to do stuff.

00:04:31.504 --> 00:04:33.139 align:start size:94% position:6%
And, you know,
I think kids are great,

00:04:33.139 --> 00:04:35.608 align:start size:94% position:6%
but I wouldn't want anything
to come between that."

00:04:35.608 --> 00:04:38.077 align:start size:94% position:6%
And they were like,
"That makes sense."

00:04:38.077 --> 00:04:39.279 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
[ Laughter ]

00:04:39.279 --> 00:04:40.113 line:92%
They were talking it out.

00:04:40.113 --> 00:04:42.415 align:start size:94% position:6%
This one girl went,
"You might like kids."

00:04:42.415 --> 00:04:45.418 align:start size:94% position:6%
And I was like, "Maybe."
And she went, "Nah."

00:04:45.418 --> 00:04:45.952 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
[ Laughter ]

00:04:45.952 --> 00:04:48.354 align:start size:94% position:6%
And then we were all doing
a shot the next day.

00:04:48.354 --> 00:04:49.355 line:92%
And my wife, Anna, came by set

00:04:49.355 --> 00:04:52.659
And she walked in and I went
"That's my wife, everybody."

00:04:52.659 --> 00:04:55.295 align:start size:94% position:6%
And everyone went,
"Hi, Mrs. Mulaney."

00:04:55.295 --> 00:04:55.795 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
[ Audience aws ]

00:04:55.795 --> 00:04:57.797 align:start size:94% position:6%
And then this little girl --
not little girl.

00:04:57.797 --> 00:05:00.366 align:start size:94% position:6%
Wonderful girl, Camille, turne
to me and said,

00:05:00.366 --> 00:05:03.202 align:start size:94% position:6%
"Does your wife
know you don't want kids?"

00:05:03.202 --> 00:05:05.038 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
[ Laughter ]

